C['gold-trading']='''<section id="overview"><h2>Project overview</h2><p>A working research prototype that collects real gold, silver and platinum observations, preserves their origin and frequency, and publishes a traceable analytical dashboard.</p><p><a href="https://intasan.github.io/gold-trading/">Open recorded-data dashboard ↗</a></p></section><section id="problem"><h2>Problem & objectives</h2><p>Spot quotes, monthly averages and reference exchange rates measure different things. The system keeps them separate so analysis does not silently mix instruments, units or time frequencies.</p></section><section id="responsibilities"><h2>My responsibilities</h2><p>Designed and implemented provider adapters, validation rules, SQL storage, read-only API, dashboard and model evaluation. This repository implementation is a research project, with no claimed client engagement or trading results.</p></section><section id="requirements"><h2>Requirements & acceptance criteria</h2><ul><li>Retain provider timestamps and response SHA-256 provenance.</li><li>Reject invalid prices, units, dates and duplicate batch keys before loading.</li><li>Make ingestion idempotent; preserve validated data during source outages and report failure explicitly.</li><li>Separate monthly prices, spot quotes and daily reference FX.</li><li>Evaluate models chronologically against a naive baseline before publishing a forecast.</li></ul><a href="https://github.com/intasan/gold-trading/blob/main/docs/ARCHITECTURE.md">Source-derived requirements, architecture, data model & API ↗</a></section><section id="workflow"><h2>System workflow</h2><ol class="flow"><li>Fetch World Bank workbook, Gold API quotes and Frankfurter FX</li><li>Validate source, unit, timestamp and finite positive value</li><li>Transactional UPSERT into SQLite</li><li>Evaluate monthly model using expanding-window validation</li><li>Publish JSON, CSV and SHA-256 manifest</li></ol></section><section id="data-model"><h2>Database & architecture</h2><p>SQLite persistence is verified. observations uses a composite key of source, series, frequency and observed_at. pipeline_runs, source_runs and model_runs preserve operational history. PostgreSQL support and an Airflow DAG are supplied but their runtime has not been tested.</p><p>The Python server exposes read-only health and snapshot endpoints. GitHub Pages serves the recorded JSON export; it does not run the Python service.</p></section><section id="implementation"><h2>Implementation & data sources</h2><p>The recorded export contains 2,403 World Bank monthly observations (801 each for gold, silver and platinum), two timestamped spot quotes and one USD/THB reference rate. Export time: 3 November 2026, 17:14:09 UTC. These are recorded observations, not current streaming prices.</p><a href="https://github.com/intasan/gold-trading/blob/main/docs/DATA_SOURCES.md">Sources, units and provenance ↗</a></section><section id="testing"><h2>Testing & validation</h2><p>Twelve unit tests passed for validation, atomicity, idempotence, outage handling, export consistency and chronological model evaluation. The actual Python HTTP server passed eight route checks. Browser Preview checks at 360, 390, 768 and 1440 CSS pixels found no horizontal overflow; physical devices were not tested.</p><a href="https://github.com/intasan/gold-trading/blob/main/evidence/IMPLEMENTATION_ACCEPTANCE.md">Implementation acceptance evidence ↗</a></section><section id="model"><h2>ML evaluation</h2><p>HistGradientBoosting uses lagged monthly gold, silver and platinum features. An expanding-window evaluation produced 36 holdout predictions for October 2023–September 2026. MAE: candidate 133.60 versus naive 129.53 USD/troy oz. The candidate did not outperform the baseline; it is not promoted and no point forecast is published.</p><p>This is retrospective evaluation on current-vintage monthly data. Publication latency is not reconstructed; it is not a point-in-time trading backtest.</p><a href="https://github.com/intasan/gold-trading/blob/main/docs/MODEL_CARD.md">Model card & methodology ↗</a></section><section id="deliverables"><h2>Results & deliverables</h2><p>Executable ingestion pipeline, SQLite schema, read-only API, real-data dashboard, downloadable observations, provenance manifest, automated checks and reproducible monthly ML evaluation.</p></section><section id="evidence"><h2>Real system evidence</h2><figure><img src="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/intasan/gold-trading/main/evidence/dashboard-desktop.jpg" alt="Actual deployed Gold dashboard showing timestamped recorded observations" loading="lazy" style="width:100%;height:auto"><figcaption>Real browser capture, 4 November 2026. Recorded export; no generated screenshot or sample market data.</figcaption></figure></section><section id="limitations"><h2>Limitations & lessons learned</h2><p>PostgreSQL, Docker and Airflow runtime remain untested. The public dashboard is a recorded export. The evaluated model loses to a simple baseline, demonstrating why honest baseline comparison and forecast gating are necessary before operational use.</p></section><a class="button solid" href="https://github.com/intasan/gold-trading">View source on GitHub ↗</a>'''
C['gold-trading']=C['gold-trading'].replace('PostgreSQL support and an Airflow DAG are supplied but their runtime has not been tested.','Docker and PostgreSQL 16.15 are verified on GitHub Actions, including replay idempotence and persistence after an actual container restart. Airflow 2.10.5 ran all three DAG tasks successfully through its DAG CLI. Airflow metadata uses isolated SQLite; business observations use PostgreSQL.').replace('2,403 World Bank monthly observations (801 each','2,406 World Bank monthly observations (802 each').replace('two timestamped spot quotes and one USD/THB reference rate','four recorded spot quotes and two USD/THB reference rates').replace('3 November 2026, 17:14:09 UTC','4 November 2026, 06:56:26 UTC').replace('October 2023–September 2026','November 2023–October 2026').replace('133.60 versus naive 129.53','138.14 versus naive 135.47').replace('This repository implementation is a research project, with no claimed client engagement or trading results.','This research project focuses on traceable data and reproducible evaluation.').replace('PostgreSQL, Docker and Airflow runtime remain untested. The public dashboard is a recorded export.','Docker, PostgreSQL and Airflow are verified in an isolated GitHub Actions runtime. Daily refresh is configured for 13:17 Asia/Bangkok and its first complete run passed through export commit and GitHub Pages rebuild. Services are ephemeral, with recorded observations persisted in Git; no continuously hosted database, Airflow UI or scheduler is claimed. The public dashboard is a recorded export.')
